AltoLeverageSwapperMultiTarget::constructor(address,address[])
├── given owner is zero even when the target list also contains zero
│   └── it should revert with OwnableInvalidOwner before target validation
└── given owner is nonzero
    ├── when any target is zero including after valid entries
    │   └── it should revert with AltoLeverageSwapperInvalidInput
    ├── when the target list is empty
    │   └── it should deploy without enabling any targets
    ├── when all targets are nonzero
    │   ├── when entries are contracts or EOAs
    │   │   └── it should mark every supplied target as valid without interface validation
    │   ├── when an address occurs more than once
    │   │   └── it should accept duplicates and emit for every occurrence
    │   └── it should emit SetValidSwapTarget with true for each entry in input order after OwnershipTransferred
    ├── it should store owner and emit OwnershipTransferred from zero to owner
    ├── it should leave owner and deployer unwhitelisted
    ├── it should leave zero and unrelated targets invalid
    └── it should emit no events beyond the ownership and per-entry target events
